// Title: Invocation of Active Directory Diagnostic Tool (ntdsutil.exe)
// Sigma ID: 2afafd61-6aae-4df4-baed-139fa1f4c345
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Thomas Patzke
// Date: 2019-01-16 | Modified: 2022-03-11
// ATT&CK: credential-access, T1003.003
// Description: Detects execution of ntdsutil.exe, which can be used for various attacks against the NTDS
//   database (NTDS.DIT)
// False positives:
//   - NTDS maintenance
// References:
//   - https://jpcertcc.github.io/ToolAnalysisResultSheet/details/ntdsutil.htm
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_ntdsutil_usage.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\ntdsutil.exe"
